<title>UK: GECC sets $250 million five-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>GECC sets $250 million five-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced</p>
<p>by lead manager SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT	  $250 MLN  COUPON     6.25	MATURITY    08.NOV.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.395   PAY DATE    08.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.77     SPREAD	+8 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIP     NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.25 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 31.OCT.01 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
